# Paths and names of any length (FIXED-BLOCKS-AUDIT; Codex, OPUS-CODEX-20261005-01
# (2) B). Each name of a field here is 600 bytes long, and the path of two
# of them is over 1200 bytes: longer than every fixed length the translator
# had for the text of a path (255, 256 and 1024 bytes). The same path is
# read and written through a declared formal (rd, wr), through a free name
# nothing in the method's sight declares (fr, fw), and in the method that
# made the copy; an element of an Array field of a long name is written
# through its address and read through a formal (el), and its length is
# read. A field of one name of that length is read through the formal (rd)
# and by its occurrence (oc); the path is read through a typed reference
# whose own name is that long, and stored into a declared field (k).
